.TH GIT-SYNC 1 "2026-11-10" "git-sync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-sync \- update all local branches from their remotes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-sync
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-sync
fetches and prunes the remote whose
.I <remote>/HEAD
ref exists (usually
.BR origin ),
then walks every local branch.
A branch that is behind its upstream, or behind the same-named branch on that
remote, is fast-forwarded.
A branch whose upstream was deleted is removed if it is merged into the
default branch.
.PP
Branches with unpushed commits, and deleted branches that are not merged,
are left alone and reported with a warning.
.PP
Tags are neither fetched nor pruned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git sync
Updated branch main (was 8915328).
Deleted branch feature-123 (was 7c24329).
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-fetch (1)
